{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc | sed -n '530,660p;800,1060p;1250,1370p;1410,1460p'\"","aggregated_output":"   530\t   Both evaluators sit behind the same two stages (yin.vm.macro.md §10.1):\n   531\t   the expander observes `program-in` — `:program-stream`, watched by\n   532\t   `:observer` — and appends each expanded tree packet to `program-out` —\n   533\t   `:row-stream`, watched independently by the evaluator's `:row-observer`,\n   534\t   which loads each packet and runs it.\n   535\t\n   536\t   The link pair is the session's (`yin.repl.link/make-pair`): the VM's\n   537\t   half lives in its private `:resources`, the interpreter's half beside\n   538\t   it under `:link-pair`.  The content pair and the name environment the\n   539\t   interpreter serves from are the shell's (`:link-source`), and outlive\n   540\t   a session rebuild.\"\n   541\t  [vm-type output-stream extra-primitives]\n   542\t  (let [pair (link/make-pair)\n   543\t        vm (make-vm vm-type output-stream extra-primitives pair)\n   544\t        program-in (make-attachment ingress-capacity)\n   545\t        program-out (make-attachment ingress-capacity)]\n   546\t    {:vm vm\n   547\t     :load-program (get program-loaders vm-type)\n   548\t     :program-stream (:stream program-in)\n   549\t     :program-identity (:identity program-in)\n   550\t     :observer (:observer program-in)\n   551\t     :expander (make-expander (:identity program-in) (:stream program-out))\n   552\t     :row-stream (:stream program-out)\n   553\t     :row-observer (:observer program-out)\n   554\t     :link-pair pair}))\n   555\t\n   556\t\n   557\t(defn- checked-link-policy\n   558\t  \"Validate the `:link-policy` creation option, failing closed at\n   559\t   assembly (yin.repl.link-policy.md section 3): `:manual` is the\n   560\t   default and today's behavior, a function `(fn [view])` is the\n   561\t   embedder's rule, and `:lease` is reserved for the phase-2 deadline --\n   562\t   refused, not implemented yet.  Anything else is refused with the\n   563\t   supported values named.\"\n   564\t  [policy]\n   565\t  (cond\n   566\t    (or (nil? policy) (= :manual policy)) :manual\n   567\t    (fn? policy) policy\n   568\t    :else\n   569\t    (throw\n   570\t      (ex-info\n   571\t        (if (= :lease policy)\n   572\t          \"Yin REPL :link-policy :lease is not implemented yet\"\n   573\t          \"Unknown Yin REPL :link-policy\")\n   574\t        {:link-policy policy\n   575\t         :supported [:manual :fn]}))))\n   576\t\n   577\t\n   578\t(defn create-state\n   579\t  \"Create the shell value.  `:primitives` is a host-supplied map merged over\n   580\t   the REPL primitives; it is kept as `:extra-primitives` so every session\n   581\t   rebuild — `(reset)`, `(vm …)` — installs it again.\n   582\t\n   583\t   `content-store` (a `dao.jing` byte-store handle), `content-client` (a\n   584\t   `dao.stream.rpc` client state on a connection whose far end serves\n   585\t   content) and `name-env` (module name -> manifest address) compose the\n   586\t   content pair and the name environment the linker interpreter serves\n   587\t   `(require ...)` from (yin.repl.link/composition); with neither content\n   588\t   source, a require stays `:pending` and says so.\n   589\t\n   590\t   `:link-policy` is the session's pending-link rule\n   591\t   (yin.repl.link-policy.md), kept beside `:link-source` so `(reset)` and\n   592\t   `(vm ...)` preserve it: `:manual`, the default, ends a pending run\n   593\t   only at `(abandon)`; a function `(fn [view])` is consulted when a\n   594\t   require parks and after each re-check that leaves the run pending,\n   595\t   answering `:keep`, `:abandon` or `{:abandon reason}`; `:lease` is\n   596\t   reserved for phase 2 and refused, as is anything else, at assembly.\"\n   597\t  ([] (create-state {}))\n   598\t  ([{:keys [lang output-cursor output-stream vm-type primitives\n   599\t            content-store content-client name-env link-policy]\n   600\t     :or {lang :clojure vm-type :semantic}}]\n   601\t   (let [output-stream (or output-stream (make-output-medium!))\n   602\t         output-cursor (or output-cursor (mint-cursor output-stream))\n   603\t         link-source (link/composition\n   604\t                       {:name-env name-env\n   605\t                        :content-store content-store\n   606\t                        :content-client content-client})]\n   607\t     (merge\n   608\t       (make-session vm-type output-stream primitives)\n   609\t       {:lang lang\n   610\t        :vm-type vm-type\n   611\t        :extra-primitives primitives\n   612\t        :output-stream output-stream\n   613\t        :output-cursor output-cursor\n   614\t        :ledger {:output :untried}\n   615\t        :shell-token (str (random-uuid))\n   616\t        :round 0\n   617\t        :ingress-loss? false\n   618\t        :last-value nil\n   619\t        :last-value-2 nil\n   620\t        :last-value-3 nil\n   621\t        :pending-input nil\n   622\t        :link-source link-source\n   623\t        :link-policy (checked-link-policy link-policy)\n   624\t        :pending-run nil\n   625\t        :running? true}))))\n   626\t\n   627\t\n   628\t;; =============================================================================\n   629\t;; Reading and classifying input\n   630\t;; =============================================================================\n   631\t\n   632\t(defn- read-forms\n   633\t  [input]\n   634\t  #?(:cljd (edn/read-string (str \"[\" input \"]\"))\n   635\t     :cljs (reader/read-string (str \"[\" input \"]\"))\n   636\t     :clj (clojure.core/read-string (str \"[\" input \"]\"))))\n   637\t\n   638\t\n   639\t(defn- command-form?\n   640\t  [form]\n   641\t  (and (seq? form)\n   642\t       (symbol? (first form))\n   643\t       (contains? command-heads (first form))))\n   644\t\n   645\t\n   646\t(defn- datom?\n   647\t  [value]\n   648\t  (and (vector? value) (= 5 (count value))))\n   649\t\n   650\t\n   651\t(defn- datom-stream?\n   652\t  [value]\n   653\t  (and (vector? value) (seq value) (every? datom? value)))\n   654\t\n   655\t\n   656\t(defn- ast-map?\n   657\t  [value]\n   658\t  (and (map? value) (keyword? (:type value))))\n   659\t\n   660\t\n   800\t   output medium.  The two stages meet only at `program-out`; neither calls\n   801\t   the other.\"\n   802\t  [{:keys [load-program output-stream] :as state}]\n   803\t  (let [{:keys [observer] vm :consumer}\n   804\t        (observer/run-on-stream {:observer (:row-observer state),\n   805\t                                 :consumer (:vm state)}\n   806\t                                engine/ready-for-ingress?\n   807\t                                load-program\n   808\t                                (make-runner output-stream (round-id state)))]\n   809\t    (assoc state :row-observer observer :vm vm)))\n   810\t\n   811\t\n   812\t(defn- format-expansion-errors\n   813\t  [errors]\n   814\t  (str/join \"\\n\" (map #(str \"Error: Macro expansion failed: \" (format-value %))\n   815\t                      errors)))\n   816\t\n   817\t\n   818\t(defn- link-waiting?\n   819\t  \"True while `vm` parks on a link wait: the two link states `require`\n   820\t   parks in, or the install it waits on (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.2).\n   821\t   These are the reasons the shell's interpreter can move, so they are\n   822\t   the ones a round drives before reporting the VM wedged.\"\n   823\t  [vm]\n   824\t  (boolean (some #(contains? #{:link-request :link-response :install}\n   825\t                             (:reason %))\n   826\t                 (:wait-set vm))))\n   827\t\n   828\t\n   829\t(defn- carry-link-identity\n   830\t  \"The round's base VM with the link identity `used` has already minted\n   831\t   carried forward: link ids `[origin counter]` and install-child origin\n   832\t   tags are minted once and never reused on a pair (yin.vm.linker.md\n   833\t   section 7.2), and the shell's rollback to the round's base -- whose\n   834\t   counters never advanced -- must not let a later require or install\n   835\t   mint an identity the pair has already answered.\"\n   836\t  [base used]\n   837\t  (let [n (max (or (:id-counter base) 0) (or (:id-counter used) 0))\n   838\t        o (max (or (:origins base) 0) (or (:origins used) 0))]\n   839\t    (cond-> base\n   840\t      (pos? n) (assoc :id-counter n)\n   841\t      (pos? o) (assoc :origins o))))\n   842\t\n   843\t\n   844\t(defn- link-raise\n   845\t  \"The raise of a resumed link wait, carrying the identity the parked\n   846\t   evaluation has minted so far -- the counters of the VM the raise\n   847\t   interrupted, whose every earlier run is in them -- so a rollback\n   848\t   cannot reuse it.\"\n   849\t  [error vm]\n   850\t  (ex-info (or (ex-message error) \"Link failed\")\n   851\t           (assoc (or (ex-data error) {})\n   852\t                  ::link-counter (:id-counter vm)\n   853\t                  ::link-origins (:origins vm))))\n   854\t\n   855\t\n   856\t(defn- drive-links\n   857\t  \"Serve the linker interpreter and run the parked VM alternately, at most\n   858\t   `link-round-budget` rounds, while `vm` waits on a link.  A round that\n   859\t   moves nothing ends the drive: a link whose content source cannot\n   860\t   answer will not answer by waiting longer.  Returns\n   861\t   `[state vm pending progress?]`, `pending` the links the interpreter\n   862\t   reported `:pending`, and `progress?` true when a round moved\n   863\t   something -- advanced a serve cursor, delivered a response or\n   864\t   completed an install -- the fact the pending run's `:checks` resets\n   865\t   on (yin.repl.link-policy.md section 3.1).  A refused or lost link\n   866\t   raises as the VM's own, carrying the interrupted VM's minted\n   867\t   identity.\"\n   868\t  [state vm]\n   869\t  (loop [i 0\n   870\t         vm vm\n   871\t         state state\n   872\t         pending []\n   873\t         progress? false]\n   874\t    (cond\n   875\t      (or (vm/halted? vm) (not (link-waiting? vm)) (>= i link-round-budget))\n   876\t      [state vm pending progress?]\n   877\t\n   878\t      :else\n   879\t      (let [served (link/serve {:pair (:link-pair state)\n   880\t                                :source (:link-source state)})\n   881\t            state (assoc state :link-pair (:pair served))\n   882\t            pending (if (seq (:pending served)) (:pending served) pending)]\n   883\t        (if (:progress? served)\n   884\t          (let [vm' (try (vm/run vm)\n   885\t                         (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error)\n   886\t                                error\n   887\t                           (throw (link-raise error vm))))]\n   888\t            (recur (inc i) vm' state pending true))\n   889\t          [state vm pending progress?])))))\n   890\t\n   891\t\n   892\t(defn- tokenize\n   893\t  \"Answer the halted VM's value on the output medium under `state`'s\n   894\t   round, as the evaluator runner does for a program it runs itself.  A\n   895\t   resumed require halts outside the observer loop, so the shell emits\n   896\t   its token here.\"\n   897\t  [state vm]\n   898\t  ((make-runner (:output-stream state) (round-id state)) vm))\n   899\t\n   900\t\n   901\t(defn- pending-text\n   902\t  [pending]\n   903\t  (if (seq pending)\n   904\t    (str \";; require pending: \"\n   905\t         (str/join \", \" (map (fn [p]\n   906\t                               (str (pr-str (:name p))\n   907\t                                    \" (link \" (pr-str (:yin.link/id p)) \")\"))\n   908\t                             pending))\n   909\t         \"); lines typed meanwhile run when it completes, (abandon) gives\"\n   910\t         \" up\\n\")\n   911\t    (str \";; require still pending; lines typed meanwhile run when it\"\n   912\t         \" completes, (abandon) gives up\\n\")))\n   913\t\n   914\t\n   915\t(defn- dropped-lines-text\n   916\t  [n]\n   917\t  (when (pos? n)\n   918\t    (str \";; dropped \" n \" line\" (when (> n 1) \"s\")\n   919\t         \" typed while the require was pending\\n\")))\n   920\t\n   921\t\n   922\t(def ^:private policy-abandon-text\n   923\t  \"The message a policy-driven abandon prints, in the shape of the\n   924\t   `(abandon)` notice, so a policy abandon is never mistaken for a\n   925\t   user's (yin.repl.link-policy.md section 3.3).\"\n   926\t  \";; the session link policy ended the require\\n\")\n   927\t\n   928\t\n   929\t(defn- abandon-pending\n   930\t  \"Give up the shell's `:pending-run` (section 7.2, step 7, the abandoned\n   931\t   case): every install in flight is dropped through the engine's own\n   932\t   `refused`, every link wait entry is retired with the reason raised as\n   933\t   the require's error, and the shell returns to the round the require\n   934\t   began in, whose store and value history the parked evaluation never\n   935\t   wrote.  Lines typed while the require was pending are dropped with\n   936\t   it, and said so.  The linker side learns nothing: no response was\n   937\t   ever promised, and one that still arrives is skipped as late.  The\n   938\t   identity the parked evaluation minted -- link ids and child origins\n   939\t   -- is carried onto the base, so nothing is minted twice on the\n   940\t   surviving pair.  The `(abandon)` command retires with\n   941\t   `:yin.repl/abandoned` and no message of its own; the session link\n   942\t   policy retires with the reason it answered and prints\n   943\t   `policy-abandon-text`, so a policy abandon is never mistaken for a\n   944\t   user's.\"\n   945\t  ([state] (abandon-pending state :yin.repl/abandoned nil))\n   946\t  ([state reason ended-text]\n   947\t   (if-let [parked (:pending-run state)]\n   948\t     (let [[state' text] (drain-output state)\n   949\t           ;; installs first: their waiters leave the wait set with the\n   950\t           ;; refusal queued, then every remaining link entry retires\n   951\t           vm (engine/abandon-installs (:vm parked) reason)\n   952\t           error (try\n   953\t                   (vm/run (reduce (fn [vm e]\n   954\t                                     (engine/abandon-link vm (:link-id e)\n   955\t                                                          reason))\n   956\t                                   vm\n   957\t                                   (:wait-set vm)))\n   958\t                   nil\n   959\t                   (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) e\n   960\t                     e))]\n   961\t       [(assoc state'\n   962\t               :vm (carry-link-identity (:base parked) vm)\n   963\t               :pending-run nil)\n   964\t        (str text\n   965\t             ended-text\n   966\t             (if error (format-error error) \"\")\n   967\t             (dropped-lines-text (count (:pending-lines parked))))])\n   968\t     [state \"Nothing is pending\"])))\n   969\t\n   970\t\n   971\t(defn- consult-link-policy\n   972\t  \"Consult the shell's `:link-policy` over a run that is still pending --\n   973\t   when the require parks, and after each re-check that leaves it so;\n   974\t   never on a re-check that completes it (yin.repl.link-policy.md\n   975\t   section 3.2).  `text` is what the round printed so far and\n   976\t   `kept-text` what a kept run reports.  `:manual` is never consulted\n   977\t   and keeps the run; a function's `:keep` keeps it; `:abandon` or\n   978\t   `{:abandon reason}` runs the same abandon path as `(abandon)`, the\n   979\t   reason defaulting to `:yin.repl/link-policy`; a throw or a return\n   980\t   outside the contract is a `:keep` for this consult plus one shell\n   981\t   error line -- never a silent abandon, never session death (section\n   982\t   3.4).  The view the function receives is plain data, no clock, no\n   983\t   handle, no secret (section 3.1).  Returns `[state text]`.\"\n   984\t  [state text kept-text]\n   985\t  (if-not (fn? (:link-policy state))\n   986\t    [state (str text kept-text)]\n   987\t    (let [parked (:pending-run state)\n   988\t          answer (try\n   989\t                   {:answer ((:link-policy state)\n   990\t                             {:links (mapv (fn [p]\n   991\t                                             {:name (:name p)\n   992\t                                              :link-id (:yin.link/id p)})\n   993\t                                           (:links parked))\n   994\t                              :checks (or (:checks parked) 0)\n   995\t                              :lines-retained\n   996\t                              (count (:pending-lines parked))})}\n   997\t                   (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) e\n   998\t                     {:thrown e}))]\n   999\t      (cond\n  1000\t        (:thrown answer)\n  1001\t        [state (str text kept-text (format-error (:thrown answer)) \"\\n\")]\n  1002\t\n  1003\t        (= :keep (:answer answer))\n  1004\t        [state (str text kept-text)]\n  1005\t\n  1006\t        (= :abandon (:answer answer))\n  1007\t        (let [[state' text'] (abandon-pending state :yin.repl/link-policy\n  1008\t                                              policy-abandon-text)]\n  1009\t          [state' (str text text')])\n  1010\t\n  1011\t        (and (map? (:answer answer)) (contains? (:answer answer) :abandon))\n  1012\t        (let [reason (or (:abandon (:answer answer)) :yin.repl/link-policy)\n  1013\t              [state' text'] (abandon-pending state reason\n  1014\t                                              policy-abandon-text)]\n  1015\t          [state' (str text text')])\n  1016\t\n  1017\t        :else\n  1018\t        [state\n  1019\t         (str text\n  1020\t              kept-text\n  1021\t              (format-error\n  1022\t                (ex-info\n  1023\t                  \"Link policy returned a value outside its contract\"\n  1024\t                  {:answer (:answer answer)\n  1025\t                   :contract [:keep :abandon {:abandon :reason}]}))\n  1026\t              \"\\n\")]))))\n  1027\t\n  1028\t\n  1029\t(defn- pending-eval\n  1030\t  \"Answer a round whose require did not complete: the parked VM, its\n  1031\t   round-start base, and the pending links are the shell's\n  1032\t   `:pending-run`, and the prompt returns.  Nothing is wedged: another\n  1033\t   line re-checks the link, the host may step one itself with\n  1034\t   `recheck-pending`, the link policy is consulted as the run parks, and\n  1035\t   `(reset)` or `(vm ...)` drops it with the session.\"\n  1036\t  [state state' vm' pending]\n  1037\t  (let [[state'' text] (drain-output state')]\n  1038\t    (consult-link-policy\n  1039\t      (assoc state''\n  1040\t             :vm vm'\n  1041\t             :pending-run {:vm vm'\n  1042\t                           :base (:vm state)\n  1043\t                           :links pending\n  1044\t                           :checks 0})\n  1045\t      text\n  1046\t      (pending-text pending))))\n  1047\t\n  1048\t\n  1049\t(defn- wedged-program\n  1050\t  [state]\n  1051\t  (ex-info\n  1052\t    \"Program stream did not form a complete, runnable Yin VM program.\n  1053\tHint: If you wanted to evaluate these datoms as data, use a quote: '[[...]]\"\n  1054\t    {:vm-type (:vm-type state)}))\n  1055\t\n  1056\t\n  1057\t(defn- run-evaluation\n  1058\t  \"The evaluator half of a round whose expander forwarded a program: run\n  1059\t   it, then either finalize the value, drive its require to a conclusion,\n  1060\t   or park it as `:pending-run`.  `state` is the round's starting state;\n  1250\t      quit [(assoc state :running? false) \"Bye\"]\n  1251\t      telemetry [state telemetry-text]\n  1252\t      [state (str \"Error: Unknown Yin REPL command \" (pr-str command))])))\n  1253\t\n  1254\t\n  1255\t(defn- eval-parsed*\n  1256\t  \"The parse dispatch of one line, against a shell with no require to\n  1257\t   re-check.\"\n  1258\t  [state trimmed parsed]\n  1259\t  (try\n  1260\t    (let [forms (:forms parsed)\n  1261\t          form (when (= 1 (count forms)) (first forms))]\n  1262\t      (cond\n  1263\t        (and form (command-form? form)) (handle-command state form)\n  1264\t        (and form (datom-stream? form)) (eval-program state (vec form))\n  1265\t        (and form (ast-map? form)) (eval-program state form)\n  1266\t        forms (if (= :clojure (:lang state))\n  1267\t                (eval-program state (compile-clojure-forms forms))\n  1268\t                (eval-program state (compile-source (:lang state) trimmed)))\n  1269\t        (= :clojure (:lang state)) [state (format-error (:error parsed))]\n  1270\t        :else (eval-program state (compile-source (:lang state) trimmed))))\n  1271\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) error\n  1272\t      (let [[state' output-text] (drain-output state)]\n  1273\t        [state' (str output-text (format-error error))]))))\n  1274\t\n  1275\t\n  1276\t(defn- fold-queued\n  1277\t  \"Evaluate the lines retained while a require was pending, in the order\n  1278\t   they were typed, each exactly once, and join their texts.  A line that\n  1279\t   parks the shell on a require of its own stops the fold: the lines\n  1280\t   after it stay retained, in order, on the new `:pending-run`.\"\n  1281\t  [[state text] queued]\n  1282\t  (loop [state state\n  1283\t         text text\n  1284\t         [in & more :as queued] (seq queued)]\n  1285\t    (cond\n  1286\t      (empty? queued) [state text]\n  1287\t      (:pending-run state) [(update-in state [:pending-run :pending-lines]\n  1288\t                                       (fnil into []) queued)\n  1289\t                            text]\n  1290\t      :else (let [[state' text'] (eval-parsed* state\n  1291\t                                               (:trimmed in)\n  1292\t                                               (:parsed in))]\n  1293\t              (recur state' (str text \"\\n\" text') more)))))\n  1294\t\n  1295\t\n  1296\t(defn- recheck-pending*\n  1297\t  \"One bounded re-check of the shell's `:pending-run`: serve the\n  1298\t   interpreter, run the parked VM, and either answer its value -- the\n  1299\t   round the require began in finally completes, and the lines retained\n  1300\t   while it was pending, then `input`, evaluate against it -- consult\n  1301\t   the link policy when the re-check leaves the run pending, `:checks`\n  1302\t   counting this pending run's re-checks that made no progress and\n  1303\t   resetting on one that did, or, when the re-check raised the link's\n  1304\t   refusal, return the shell to the round's base with the error as text\n  1305\t   and evaluate `input` there.  `input` is nil for the host's\n  1306\t   `recheck-pending`, which evaluates no line of its own.\"\n  1307\t  [state input]\n  1308\t  (let [parked (:pending-run state)]\n  1309\t    (try\n  1310\t      (let [[state' vm' pending progress?] (drive-links state (:vm parked))]\n  1311\t        (if (vm/halted? vm')\n  1312\t          (let [vm'' (engine/restore-initial-env (:env (:base parked)) vm')\n  1313\t                [st text] (finalize-eval state\n  1314\t                                         (assoc state' :vm vm'')\n  1315\t                                         (tokenize state' vm''))]\n  1316\t            (fold-queued [(assoc st :vm vm'' :pending-run nil) text]\n  1317\t                         (cond-> (vec (:pending-lines parked))\n  1318\t                           input (conj input))))\n  1319\t          (let [checks (if progress? 0 (inc (or (:checks parked) 0)))\n  1320\t                parked' (cond-> (assoc parked\n  1321\t                                       :vm vm'\n  1322\t                                       :links pending\n  1323\t                                       :checks checks)\n  1324\t                          input (update :pending-lines\n  1325\t                                        (fnil conj []) input))\n  1326\t                [st text] (drain-output (assoc state'\n  1327\t                                               :vm vm'\n  1328\t                                               :pending-run parked'))]\n  1329\t            (consult-link-policy st text (pending-text pending)))))\n  1330\t      (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) error\n  1331\t        (let [[st text] (drain-output state)\n  1332\t              d (ex-data error)]\n  1333\t          (fold-queued\n  1334\t            [(assoc st\n  1335\t                    :vm (carry-link-identity\n  1336\t                          (:base parked)\n  1337\t                          {:id-counter (::link-counter d)\n  1338\t                           :origins (::link-origins d)})\n  1339\t                    :pending-run nil)\n  1340\t             (str text\n  1341\t                  (format-error error)\n  1342\t                  (dropped-lines-text (count (:pending-lines parked))))]\n  1343\t            (cond-> [] input (conj input))))))))\n  1344\t\n  1345\t\n  1346\t(defn recheck-pending\n  1347\t  \"One re-check of the shell's `:pending-run` without an input line --\n  1348\t   the step an unattended host drives at its own cadence\n  1349\t   (yin.repl.link-policy.md section 4): serve the interpreter, run the\n  1350\t   parked VM, and consult the link policy when the run is still\n  1351\t   pending.  A re-check that completes the run folds the retained lines\n  1352\t   exactly as a typed line's completion does.  Returns `[state text]`,\n  1353\t   `text` nil when nothing is pending.  It reads no clock and takes no\n  1354\t   callback; the host decides when to call it.\"\n  1355\t  [state]\n  1356\t  (if (:pending-run state)\n  1357\t    (recheck-pending* state nil)\n  1358\t    [state nil]))\n  1359\t\n  1360\t\n  1361\t(defn- resume-pending\n  1362\t  \"One bounded re-check of the shell's `:pending-run` behind a typed\n  1363\t   line: while the run stays pending the line is retained -- the parked\n  1364\t   VM owns the store a new evaluation would fork -- and it evaluates,\n  1365\t   in typing order and exactly once, when the link completes.\"\n  1366\t  [state trimmed parsed]\n  1367\t  (recheck-pending* state {:trimmed trimmed, :parsed parsed}))\n  1368\t\n  1369\t\n  1370\t(defn- command-line?\n  1410\t(defn repl-state\n  1411\t  \"A serializable summary of shell state.\n  1412\t\n  1413\t   The stream summaries read the ledger rather than asking a handle whether it\n  1414\t   is closed: dao.stream has no `closed?`, and an idle medium has no last\n  1415\t   operation.\n  1416\t   The program media are the composition's own, observed beside the VM, so\n  1417\t   the shell reports what it knows of them — the declared capacity, the gaps\n  1418\t   the session's observers counted, and whether a loss has already refused\n  1419\t   further evaluation.  Each `:pending` entry carries the link policy's\n  1420\t   name (`:manual` or `:fn`) and the pending run's `:checks`, so a host\n  1421\t   can display why a run is still waiting (yin.repl.link-policy.md\n  1422\t   section 3.5).  `:macros` maps each macro the expander's store holds\n  1423\t   to its lambda's root address (yin.vm.macro.md §10.1).\"\n  1424\t  [state]\n  1425\t  {:lang (:lang state)\n  1426\t   :macros (into (sorted-map-by #(compare (str %1) (str %2)))\n  1427\t                 (map (fn [[sym entry]]\n  1428\t                        [sym (first (:yin.macro/tree entry))]))\n  1429\t                 (get-in state [:expander :ctx :store]))\n  1430\t   :vm {:type (:vm-type state)\n  1431\t        :halted? (vm/halted? (:vm state))\n  1432\t        :blocked? (vm/blocked? (:vm state))\n  1433\t        :in-stream {:capacity ingress-capacity\n  1434\t                    :gaps (ingress-gaps state)\n  1435\t                    :lost? (boolean (:ingress-loss? state))}}\n  1436\t   :running? (:running? state)\n  1437\t   :output {:cursor (:output-cursor state)\n  1438\t            :last-outcome (get-in state [:ledger :output] :untried)}\n  1439\t   :pending (when-let [parked (:pending-run state)]\n  1440\t              (let [policy (:link-policy state)]\n  1441\t                (mapv (fn [p]\n  1442\t                        {:name (:name p)\n  1443\t                         :link-id (:yin.link/id p)\n  1444\t                         :policy (if (fn? policy) :fn policy)\n  1445\t                         :checks (or (:checks parked) 0)})\n  1446\t                      (:links parked))))\n  1447\t   :telemetry {:supported? false :note telemetry-text}\n  1448\t   :remote {:connected? false}})\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
